* Add more filesystem options to mkfs.briefs as they become available.
* [Done] Make man pages.  Each command has a hidden --generate-man-page
  flag (wired through urfave/cli-docs/v3) that writes a section-8 man page
  to man/man8/<name>.8; `make man` regenerates all three.
* [Done] The codebase was feeling a bit hairy, so it got another round of
  refactoring: the bu-refactor-1 branch (27 commits, not yet merged) deduplicated
  the trie/btree/journal/xattr walkers into shared briefs helpers, wired up
  fsck --verbose, removed the dead code, fixed the fsck scan hot spots, ported
  the kernel's replay generation guards and trie sibling-chain caps, and closed
  the FUSE feature gaps (all five fallocate modes, POSIX ACLs, FITRIM/FSLABEL
  ioctls, the unwritten-extent metadata reserve).
* [Done] The FUSE bridge is read-write: full kernel parity
  (all dir/file ops, xattrs, ACLs, fileattr/chattr, renameat2, fallocate/
  setattr/killpriv), Go journal port, per-inode-block locking. Still
  experimental — see xfstests-fuse-status.md for the xfstests pass/fail
  record and known issues.
* The FUSE bridge should support the same mount options as the kernel module.
* Expand xfstests coverage for BrieFS under FUSE: the replay-sensitive subset
  (generic/003, 029, 030, 032, 321, 322, 547, 640, 475, 011) currently gives
  7 PASS / 2 FAIL (generic/547, 011) / 1 NOT RUN (generic/032, fiemap
  unsupported) under the FUSE bridge — the 2026-08-06 record; the bridge has
  since gained the fallocate modes, ACLs, and FITRIM/FSLABEL ioctls on
  bu-refactor-1, not yet re-run under xfstests. (A prior "10/10 PASS" result
  was invalid — the harness was mounting via the kernel module, not the FUSE
  bridge; see the correction note in xfstests-fuse-status.md.) Broaden to
  the full generic group.
* Implement the remaining ioctls in the FUSE bridge: fiemap (FS_IOC_FIEMAP,
  which gates generic/032 to NOT RUN) and the file-range exchange ioctls
  (XFS_IOC_EXCHANGE_RANGE/SWAP_RANGE and COMMIT_RANGE — a ~500-line
  two-inode port of the kernel's briefs_do_exchange; rationale in
  fuse/ioctl_mount.go). O_TMPFILE is not bridge-addressable: the 6.12 FUSE
  client has no O_TMPFILE support.
* Port the kernel's replay trie-block reuse pool + per-directory partial-pool
  seeding (briefs_trie_seed_pool) into the FUSE replay, so crash-replay on a
  near-full filesystem reuses JRN_TRIE_ALLOC blocks instead of allocating fresh
  ones (avoids orphan trie blocks / -ENOSPC; matches the kernel's generic/475
  full-fs behaviour).
* [Done for xfstests] mkfs.briefs and fsck.briefs command line flags are
  sufficiently xfstests-compatible (force flag `-f`, check-only default,
  `-r -y` repair shape). Further standards alignment may be useful.
* [Done] Make journal size configurable.
